    fix(executor/raw): decode gzip response bodies correctly
    
    Previously the entire raw HTTP response (headers + body) was converted
    via String::from_utf8_lossy before splitting head/body, which
    irreversibly corrupted binary gzip bodies into U+FFFD replacement
    characters before any decompression could happen.
    
    - split header/body on raw bytes instead of lossy-decoded text
    - decode_chunked now operates on &[u8]
    - add decode_gzip (flate2::read::GzDecoder), applied after dechunking
    - falls back to raw bytes on decompress failure, so non-gzip responses
      are unaffected
    
    Fixes evaluator regex not matching on CVE-2024-27348 (HugeGraph) and
    any other lab where the target returns Content-Encoding: gzip.

